00:20:54,560 --> 00:21:12,820
Every day I had always loved to go to her class. She had an impact on me rather than the content she was teaching. So I think that's very important for a student-teacher relationship and helpful for a student to learn.

148
00:21:12,820 --> 00:21:36,240
So these changes with the Wynn classes is they're adding a unified arts teacher as the Wynn teacher for this period. So it's almost like it used to be a study hall. Now it's more helping the kids with what they need from a teacher's perspective versus their perspective.

149
00:21:36,240 --> 00:22:01,200
So at the beginning of the class, some kids who need help with ELA and reading, they'll do an extra 20 minutes of reading before the class, or they'll do extra math practice with these unified teachers who may not be specializing in this subject, but they're connecting with students, which is really important, and they're building good relationships.

150
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:19,140
So this is to have more comfort for unified arts and more comfort for the kids in the unified art classes and expanding, you know, teacher-student relationships throughout the team, which I think is really good.

151
00:22:19,600 --> 00:22:28,480
It's very, I'd be very happy to hear that because my brother was talking to me about it the other day, and he was like, oh, now I have to read and win class.

152
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:29,360
And he's all mad.

153
00:22:31,720 --> 00:22:36,800
I said, well, it's going to help you in the long run when you actually do have to read a book for us.

154
00:22:40,960 --> 00:22:56,660
Over in Danville, they had their first whole school assembly. They discussed safety, ownership, ambition, and respect. And on Tuesday, they had an event called Popsicles with principals. I thought this was really interesting.

155
00:22:56,660 --> 00:23:12,360
So I emailed the principal at Danville for a little more information, and she said that this is going to be a month-to-month event with parents and kids coming in, and they're going to meet with the admin team for any questions.

156
00:23:12,360 --> 00:23:29,200
They're going to socialize. So this one was, they had Popsicles. They were out on the playground. It was music. The kids were playing. The parents and the admin was able to discuss any questions, get more socializing.

157
00:23:29,200 --> 00:23:42,920
And next month, they're doing apples with admins. So they're going to have apple cider donuts and apple cider. And I thought this was a really interesting idea that they had. I thought it was pretty cool.

158
00:23:42,920 --> 00:23:49,060
So that will happen every month. There'll be a new fun name I get to share.

159
00:23:49,060 --> 00:24:03,840
So Sandown North, they've been continuing their Monday morning meetings, and they're talking about the implementations of what's going to be discussed in the classrooms Tuesday through Friday.

160
00:24:03,840 --> 00:24:17,100
They come together for about 15 minutes on Monday. They do the Pledge of Allegiance. They do grade-level roll call, weekly focus and shout-outs from the students and the staff, and they end with an activity.

161
00:24:17,100 --> 00:24:27,720
So I think this is a really good idea, and I like how consistent they are, because Mondays can be a difficult day for students. I mean, they're difficult for me.

162
00:24:28,380 --> 00:24:40,060
So getting them socializing and together at the same time in the morning is very good for them, and getting them awake for the day and the rest of the week.

163
00:24:40,060 --> 00:24:45,920
They're excited to go into school on Monday with this. They get to see their friends right as they walk through the door.

164
00:24:46,560 --> 00:24:53,400
So I thought this was a very exciting idea that they had, doing these assemblies.

165
00:24:55,340 --> 00:25:05,080
Sandown Central, Nurse Meg visited all the early childhood classes and kind of went through the different tools that she uses to, I guess,

166
00:25:05,080 --> 00:25:16,660
have the kids have the kids not be so scared, because a thermometer and the fingertip pulse can be scary for a five-year-old, I'd say.

167
00:25:18,100 --> 00:25:22,160
Kindergarten started using their Chromebooks, and they began health classes.

168
00:25:23,440 --> 00:25:30,020
And then beginning on October 5th, they're doing community playgroups.

169
00:25:30,020 --> 00:25:33,180
