948
01:10:45,680 --> 01:10:46,680
CORRECTLY.

949
01:10:46,680 --> 01:10:51,680
ONGOING, AFTER THEY'RE STARTED UP AND ONLINE, IN-HOUSE WILL BE DOING THE MAINTENANCE.

950
01:10:51,680 --> 01:10:52,680
IN-HOUSE.

951
01:10:52,680 --> 01:10:53,680
OKAY.

952
01:10:53,680 --> 01:10:55,680
THIS IS WHAT I WANT TO BRING UP TO THE TABLE.

953
01:10:55,680 --> 01:10:59,680
IS THAT DURING WHEN I WAS ON THE BOARD IN THE TENURE, DURING THE COVID ERA, WHEN OF COURSE AIR HANDLING

954
01:10:59,680 --> 01:11:05,680
BECAME THE VERY BIG TOPIC, WE DID A LOT OF STUDIES OF EVERY ONE OF THE AIR HANDLES IN HERE.

955
01:11:05,680 --> 01:11:10,680
WE HAD SOME OF THESE AIR HANDLERS THAT HAVE SAID THAT THEY HAD MAINTENANCE DONE ON THEM THROUGH

956
01:11:10,680 --> 01:11:13,680
THE LOGS OF FACILITIES AND SO FORTH.

957
01:11:13,680 --> 01:11:18,680
BUT WHEN WE HAD THE COMPANY COME THROUGH HERE AND DO AN ASSESSMENT OF THAT, WHICH WAS TRAINED,

958
01:11:18,680 --> 01:11:24,680
THERE WAS MANY OF THEM THAT WERE REPORTED THAT THERE WAS NO CONCEIVABLE MAINTENANCE THAT WAS

959
01:11:24,680 --> 01:11:25,680
PERFORMED ON THERE.

960
01:11:25,680 --> 01:11:29,680
WHICH MEANS TO ME THAT SAYS THAT THIS UNIT PROBABLY NEVER HAD THE MAINTENANCE.

961
01:11:29,680 --> 01:11:34,680
SOMEBODY WAS PROBABLY SAYING THAT IT WAS DONE AND WHEN IT WASN'T DONE.

962
01:11:34,680 --> 01:11:38,680
AND WHAT WE WANTED TO DO IS, AT THAT TIME, WE ASKED THE SUPERINTENDENT TO MAKE SURE HOW DO YOU,

963
01:11:38,680 --> 01:11:41,680
LET'S FILL THIS HOLE AND MAKE SURE THAT WE HAVE THAT DONE.

964
01:11:41,680 --> 01:11:46,680
SO I WANTED TO BRING IT TO YOUR ATTENTION SO THAT YOU CAN HAVE PROCESSES IN PLACE,

965
01:11:46,680 --> 01:11:49,680
BECAUSE I DON'T KNOW WHAT WAS ACTUALLY DONE AT THAT TIME,

966
01:11:49,680 --> 01:11:55,680
TO MAKE SURE THAT THESE MAINTENANCE IS ACTUALLY DONE SO THAT WE DON'T GET DOWN THERE 10 YEARS, 15 YEARS

967
01:11:55,680 --> 01:12:01,680
FROM NOW AND FIND OUT THAT IT'S CAKED AND DUST AND SO FORTH.

968
01:12:01,680 --> 01:12:09,680
ACTUALLY WHAT WE WILL BE DOING IS, WE STARTED ON THE UNITS THAT HAVE BEEN INSTALLED

969
01:12:09,680 --> 01:12:14,680
THE PAST FEW YEARS WITH PUTTING BARCODES ON THE UNITS SO THE TECHS CAN SCAN THOSE

970
01:12:14,680 --> 01:12:16,680
AND THEY PUT THEM INTO OUR WORKORDER SYSTEM.

971
01:12:16,680 --> 01:12:21,680
SO AS A REMINDER THAT WILL POP UP EACH YEAR, THIS UNIT HAS TO BE, YOU KNOW,

972
01:12:21,680 --> 01:12:25,680
PREVENTATIVE MAINTENANCE TAKEN CARE OF ON IT, THE FILTERS NEED TO BE CHANGED.

973
01:12:25,680 --> 01:12:31,680
AND THAT'S GREAT TO SEE THAT THERE'S SOMETHING TO BE, I COULDN'T TELL IF IT WAS DUE TO JUST,

974
01:12:31,680 --> 01:12:37,680
NOBODY KNEW ABOUT IT KIND OF THING, OR THERE WAS, YOU KNOW, BASICALLY SOMEBODY THAT DIDN'T WANT TO WORK, PERIOD.

975
01:12:37,680 --> 01:12:45,680
WHAT FLAVOR IT FELL INTO, WE DON'T KNOW, BUT THE END RESULT WAS THAT THE UNIT WASN'T UPDATED AND DONE ITS MAINTENANCE.

976
01:12:45,680 --> 01:12:46,680
THAT'S THE KEY PART.

977
01:12:46,680 --> 01:12:49,680
AND AS LONG AS THE MAINTENANCE GETS DONE, THAT'S, I THINK, ALL WE WANT.

978
01:12:49,680 --> 01:12:51,680
WE WANT TO MAKE SURE THAT WE GETS DONE.

979
01:12:51,680 --> 01:12:52,680
WE'LL BE KEEPING UP ON.

980
01:12:52,680 --> 01:12:53,680
DON, THEN JACK.

981
01:12:53,680 --> 01:13:00,680
MY RECOLLECTION OF THAT SITUATION OVER THE COURSE OF YEARS THERE WAS A LOT OF TIMES THE PARTS WERE NOT AVAILABLE,

982
01:13:00,680 --> 01:13:05,680
OR AT LEAST NOT AVAILABLE AT A TIME FRAME THAT WORK WAS GETTING DONE.

983
01:13:05,680 --> 01:13:10,680
BUT REPORTS WERE BEING MADE, AND WORK ORDERS WERE BEING, YOU KNOW, PROCESSED.

984
01:13:10,680 --> 01:13:15,680
BUT NO WORK WAS GETTING DONE BECAUSE WE DIDN'T HAVE THE PARTS TO DO IT.

985
01:13:15,680 --> 01:13:19,680
SO YOU HAD A WILLING WORK FORCE WHO HAD DIAGNOSED THE PROBLEMS, BUT THEY WEREN'T.

986
01:13:19,680 --> 01:13:21,680
IF I RECALL CORRECTLY, IT WAS AWESOME.

987
01:13:21,680 --> 01:13:23,680
I MEAN, I CAN SEE IF YOU'RE TALKING ABOUT INTERNAL PARTS.

988
01:13:23,680 --> 01:13:24,680
I'M TALKING ABOUT ALL OUR...

989
01:13:24,680 --> 01:13:28,680
JUST THE SCREENS, THE FILTERS WERE NOT REQUESTED.

990
01:13:28,680 --> 01:13:31,680
WE HAVE PROBLEMS WITH THEM TO CERTAIN DEGREES.

991
01:13:31,680 --> 01:13:34,680
SOME WERE END OF LIFE, AND OTHERS WERE ON THE WAY.

992
01:13:34,680 --> 01:13:42,680
BUT THE BIGGEST PROBLEM WAS NOT JUST DIAGNOSING THE PROBLEM, IT WAS GETTING, YOU KNOW, DELIVERY OF THE THINGS THAT THEY NEEDED TO DO THE WORK.

993
01:13:42,680 --> 01:13:48,680
SO THE PIECES, THE PARTS, YOU KNOW, THESE OLD MACHINES WERE NOT BEING SOLD ANYMORE.

994
01:13:48,680 --> 01:13:51,680
THEY WERE NOT BEING SERVICED AS MUCH ANYMORE.

995
01:13:51,680 --> 01:13:54,680
YOU KNOW, IT WAS A NIGHTMARE.

996
01:13:54,680 --> 01:13:56,680
JACK.

997
01:13:56,680 --> 01:14:00,680
MARK, YOU'RE A BREATH OF FRESH AIR.

998
01:14:00,680 --> 01:14:03,680
MARK IS EXTREMELY...I WORK WITH THEM ON THE CIP.

999
01:14:03,680 --> 01:14:06,680
I WORK WITH THEM ON FACILITIES.

1000
01:14:06,680 --> 01:14:18,680
WE WENT OUT, LOOKED AT SOME ELEVATIONS THIS MORNING TO ANSWER A FEW QUESTIONS THAT CAME UP YESTERDAY'S MEETING, OR TUESDAY'S MEETING.

1001
01:14:18,680 --> 01:14:25,680
THE ENTHUSIASM IN WHICH YOU HAVE ENTERED INTO THIS POSITION IS GREATLY APPRECIATED BY ME.

1002
01:14:25,680 --> 01:14:26,680
YOU'RE APPROACHABLE.

1003
01:14:26,680 --> 01:14:31,680
I'VE GOT NOTHING BUT POSITIVE FEEDBACK FROM, YOU KNOW, PEOPLE LIKE, OH, THIS IS GREAT.

1004
01:14:31,680 --> 01:14:42,680
SO, QUITE FRANKLY, WHEN WE DID THE WALK THROUGH IN POLIT, AND I TOLD SOMEONE TODAY, I SAID, I PUT 10 BUCKS ON VEGAS THAT THAT BUILDING WOULD NOT BE DONE ON TIME.

1005
01:14:42,680 --> 01:14:45,680
AND YOU KNOW WHAT, WE GOT THE SCHOOL OPEN.

1006
01:14:45,680 --> 01:14:48,680
IT WAS A TON OF WORK.

1007
01:14:48,680 --> 01:14:55,680
AND RELATIVE TO WHAT WE HAVE GOING ON NOW, YOU'RE LOOKING AT 200, 300 MILLION FOR NEW HIGH SCHOOL.

1008
01:14:55,680 --> 01:15:02,680
AND I'LL TALK ABOUT IT ON THE CIP REPORT IN A BIT, BUT WE ARE GETTING THERE.

1009
01:15:02,680 --> 01:15:06,680
WE ARE GETTING A TON OF WORK DONE OVER THE LAST FIVE YEARS.

1010
01:15:06,680 --> 01:15:14,680
YOU KNOW, THESE LISTS OF THINGS THAT WERE ESSENTIAL TO GET DONE HAVE DWINDLED DOWN TO ALMOST NOTHING.

1011
01:15:14,680 --> 01:15:25,680
AND I THINK, AS IT SPEAKS TO, SEAN, YOUR CONCERN, AS MUCH AS IT PAINED ME TO PUT THE CONTROLS IN, I THINK THE CONTROLS, IF I'M NOT MISTAKING, MARK, AND YOU CAN HELP ME WITH THIS,

1012
01:15:25,680 --> 01:15:35,680
IF SOMETHING ISN'T RUNNING VERY EFFICIENTLY, DOESN'T SOMETHING, AN ALARM GO OFF SOMEWHERE SAYING, HEY, YOU HAVE A PROBLEM IN THIS SECTION OR IN THIS AREA OF DUCKWORK?

1013
01:15:35,680 --> 01:15:41,680
ON THE SCHEDULED MAINTENANTS WHICH WE'RE DOCUMENTING NEEDS TO BE DONE, TO YOUR POINT, JOHN.

1014
01:15:41,680 --> 01:15:47,680
YES, OUR HVAC TECH GETS A, ON THE BMS SYSTEM, WE HAVE AN APP.

1015
01:15:47,680 --> 01:16:03,680
HE HAS AN APP ON HIS PHONE, SO IT'LL ALERT HIM OR SET AN ALARM ON HIS PHONE THAT PAUL AT SCHOOL, AND IT'LL SHOW YOU EXACTLY WHAT UNIT IS HAVING AN ISSUE, AND HE CAN DETERMINE OR TROUBLESHOOT WHAT THE ISSUE IS AT THE TIME.

1016
01:16:03,680 --> 01:16:15,680
AND I THINK THE OTHER THING, IF YOU CAN SPEAK ABOUT IT OR YOU DON'T HAVE TO, BUT WE HAVE DISCUSSED ABOUT DOING THE FACILITIES AUDIT, WHICH WILL MAKE THINGS PRETTY MUCH, THIS IS WHEN IT'S GOT TO BE DONE, THIS IS WHEN IT'S GOT TO BE.

1017
01:16:15,680 --> 01:16:27,680
INSTEAD OF FINDING OURSELVES IN THE HOLE AT SOME POINT IN TIME IN THE FUTURE, IT'S A MORE GRADUATED PROCESS OF KEEPING UP WITH THINGS, SO WHEN YOU DO THAT, COSTS GO DOWN, NOT UP.

1018
01:16:27,680 --> 01:16:41,680
AND WE'RE DOING ALL OF THAT, I THINK, IT'S FAIR TO SAY, TO MITIGATE THE IMPACT FROM A DOLLARS IN SET STANDPOINT THAT COSTLY 650,000 SQUARE FEET OF BUILDING.

1019
01:16:41,680 --> 01:16:43,680
AND BY THE WAY, THE FIELDS LOOK GOOD, TOO.

1020
01:16:43,680 --> 01:16:47,680
SO THANK YOU FOR STEPPING UP AND STEPPING IN.

1021
01:16:47,680 --> 01:16:52,680
MARK, THE BUILDING MANAGEMENT SYSTEM, HOW COMPLEX IS THAT?

1022
01:16:52,680 --> 01:17:01,680
AND WHERE I'M GOING WITH THIS IS, I KNOW THAT, YOU KNOW, FOR ELECTRICAL SUPPLY, AND WE JUST TALKED IN HERE, WE UPGRADED SOMETHING FROM 800 AMPS TO 3, 1200 AMPS.

1023
01:17:01,680 --> 01:17:05,680
AND WE'RE TAKING MORE POWER INTO THESE SYSTEMS, ALL THAT STUFF.

1024
01:17:05,680 --> 01:17:11,680
AND OUR ENERGY BILLS, OF COURSE, ARE, YOU KNOW, WE'RE COMMERCIAL RATES, SO THAT YOU'RE GOING TO BE PAYING ON DEMAND.

1025
01:17:11,680 --> 01:17:17,680
AND BUILDING MANAGEMENT SYSTEMS ARE SOPHISTICATED ENOUGH WHERE THEY'LL SORT OF REGULATE SO THAT EVERYBODY IS GOING TO BE PAYING ON DEMAND.

1026
01:17:17,680 --> 01:17:19,680
THERE'S NOBODY CALLING ON FOR AIR CONDITIONERS NOW.

1027
01:17:19,680 --> 01:17:30,680
THEY'LL REGULATE IT, LET YOU GO FOR 15 MINUTES, AND THE OTHER ONES WILL GO ON OVER HERE, AND THEN JUST SORT OF BALANCE THE LOAD SO THAT YOU'RE NOT, HEY, GET IT ALL AT PEAK DEMAND, PAYING TOP DOLLAR FOR IT.

1028
01:17:30,680 --> 01:17:33,680
ARE WE HOOKED UP LIKE THAT INTO OUR SYSTEM?

1029
01:17:33,680 --> 01:17:39,680
AND WE'VE ALSO SET, WE HAVE SET POINTS SET FOR EACH CLASSROOM, BETWEEN 68 AND 72.

1030
01:17:39,680 --> 01:17:43,680
SO IF SOMEBODY WANTS IT, YOU CANNOT GO BELOW 16.

1031
01:17:43,680 --> 01:17:47,680
I DON'T KNOW, I UNDERSTAND THAT THAT'S JUST CONTROLLING THE TEMPERATURE ASPECT.

1032
01:17:47,680 --> 01:17:52,680
BUT SAY FOR EXAMPLE, IT GETS DOWN, IT GETS TOO HOT IN HERE, IT CALLS FOR AIR CONDITIONING RIGHT NOW IN THIS ROOM.

1033
01:17:52,680 --> 01:17:53,680
RIGHT.

1034
01:17:53,680 --> 01:18:02,680
IT MIGHT SAY THE BUILDING MANAGEMENT SYSTEM MIGHT SAY, I CAN'T DO YOU RIGHT THIS MOMENT IN TIME, BUT THREE MINUTES FROM NOW I'M GOING TO BE SHUTTING ON OFF THE HIGH SCHOOL.

1035
01:18:02,680 --> 01:18:11,680
SO THAT LOAD'S GOING TO COME ON OFF, THIS ONE'S GOING TO KICK ON, AND FROM A POWER VIEWPOINT, WE'RE CONSISTENTLY WITH A LOWER AMOUNT OF POWER

1036
01:18:11,680 --> 01:18:17,680
VERSUS BEING ALL SPIKED ON OFF, PAYING THE HIGHEST RATES, AND THEN SOMETIME LATER WE ALL COME TO CRASH IT DOWN.

1037
01:18:17,680 --> 01:18:24,680
YOU USE THE SAME AMOUNT OF POWER, BUT IT'S HOW IT'S DELIVERED AND WHEN IT'S DONE, BECAUSE THAT'S WHY THEY CHARGE YOU ON DEMAND.

1038
01:18:24,680 --> 01:18:25,680
RIGHT.

1039
01:18:25,680 --> 01:18:27,680
SO DO WE TAKE ADVANTAGE OF THAT?

1040
01:18:27,680 --> 01:18:28,680
WE DO.

1041
01:18:28,680 --> 01:18:29,680
OKAY.

1042
01:18:29,680 --> 01:18:30,680
THANK YOU.

